    "language": "en",
    "description": "The Ask Suicide-Screening Questions (asQ; Horowitz et al., 2012) is a brief, clinician-administered suicide risk screening tool for use with individuals aged 8 and older. The asQ comprises four core screening questions, along with a fifth acuity question that grades the urgency of a positive screen. Developed at the United States National Institute of Mental Health (NIMH), it is included as the key component of the NIMH asQ Toolkit (National Institute of Mental Health, n.d.).",
